                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I read the novel by H G Wells well over 45 years ago and remember being slightly disturbed by it, particularly the section on vivisection (I wanted to be a vet when I was young) and the idea of vivisection was anathema to me. The novel as a whole was a book that you read and then found yourself thinking about for a long time afterwards - all power to Mr Wells then.\nNow what you ask has this to do with the game...WELL I answer - it is having the same sort of effect on me as the novel did. I haven't played it for long, and have managed to die on every attempt so far, but the way  the developers have brought to life the island is just brilliant and top marks  to them for doing so, and managing to convey the Gothic horror of the place.\nI find myself wondering just what is waiting for me around every corner, and wanting to find out but not wanting to find out at the same time! \nThat this game has been produced by an Indie and not one of the major studios speaks volumes for their expertise and abilities - so ladies and gents - whoever you are and wherever you are - take a bow.\nA really good, atmospheric game and worth every penny of its asking price.",
